<task id="090" project="email-communication-solution-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Project wrap-up — README → Complete, lessons-learned, `/test-diet` gate, archive, final code-review</title>
    <phase>Wrap-up</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>4</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>060, 061, 062, 070, 071, 072, 073, 074, 075, 076, 080, 081, 082</dependencies>
    <blocks></blocks>
    <tags>wrapup</tags>
    <rigor-hint>STANDARD</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Project-close orchestration: status flip, lessons-learned, mandatory `/test-diet` reconciliation gate (root §7), artifact archive, and a final holistic `code-review`. Writes to `.claude/`-adjacent project state + invokes gates — MUST run from the main session. STANDARD rigor with an explicit test-diet gate.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Main-session-only: runs the `/test-diet` gate, updates project state, and produces the final review after ALL work tasks complete. Cannot be delegated to a subagent (touches project-close state + gates).</parallel-reason>
    <fr-refs></fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Close out email-communication-solution-r4 from the MAIN SESSION only:

    1. **README → Complete** — flip the project README status to Complete; summarize what shipped (W0–W8) and the graduation criteria met.

    2. **Lessons-learned** — create `notes/lessons-learned.md` capturing what went well / poorly, the R3-absorption experience, the Services/Ai gate coordination, the two Microsoft deadlines, and any deferred items.

    3. **`/test-diet` gate (MANDATORY, root §7)** — invoke `/test-diet` to reconcile every test added/modified during R4 against the ADR-038 build-vs-maintain classifier: MAINTAIN-class tests stay at KEEP paths; SCAFFOLDING-class tests are emitted for deletion (`git rm`); AMBIGUOUS require reviewer judgment. The skill is read-only — it emits commands for the reviewer. Output: `notes/test-diet-report.md`. The wrap-up PR MUST cite this report.

    4. **Archive artifacts** — move ephemeral working files to the archive per `/repo-cleanup` conventions; keep permanent artifacts (spec, plan, tasks, arch docs).

    5. **Final `code-review`** — run a final holistic `code-review` across the R4 diff surface as a project-close quality gate.

    Then confirm the project is complete and ready for `merge-to-master`.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke project lead running the main-session project-close protocol. Authoritative on the wrap-up sequence, the `/test-diet` gate (root §7), `/repo-cleanup`, and the final `code-review` gate. Does NOT delegate to subagents.
  </role>

  <goal>
    README status is Complete; `notes/lessons-learned.md` and `notes/test-diet-report.md` exist; the `/test-diet` gate has run and its report is cited; ephemeral artifacts are archived; a final `code-review` has run with Critical findings addressed. The project is ready to merge to master.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      This is the project-close task. Per root §7, a `090-wrapup-*` task invokes `/test-diet` before marking the project complete — reconciling R4's test additions against the ADR-038 KEEP-path categories. R4 was large (W0–W8, absorbed R3, BFF + client + Dataverse + AI + add-in + docs), so the lessons-learned and final review are substantive.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/email-communication-solution-r4/README.md</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-solution-r4/notes/lessons-learned.md (NEW)</file>
